## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Dependencies**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to package.json
- Installed package using npm, updating package-lock.json

**2. Modified Files**
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component to the root layout

**3. Configuration Details**
- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the body of the root layout
- Followed official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router setup

### Implementation Notes

- Used the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Followed Next.js App Router pattern (not Pages Router)
- Placed Analytics component at the end of the body tag as recommended
- Build completed successfully with no errors
- Linter passed with no issues
- All lock files properly updated

### Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy to Vercel
2. Enable Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard
3. Verify analytics are being collected by checking the Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

The Analytics component will automatically track page views and Web Vitals once deployed to Vercel.
